  "caveats": [
    "Diagnostic clocks/counters and changed host code can perturb execution; no clean throughput claim.",
    "Owner queue/body/return partition each measured synchronous handoff; runtime spans are nested and must not be added to owner body.",
    "Completion wait includes GPU execution and OS scheduling, not pure CPU work or pure notification latency.",
    "Timed wall-clock spans include preemption and measurement overhead; counter updates are excluded from their own spans.",
    "Preparation/init/prefill excluded; one fixed Short, no model/MTP or math ISA changes.",
    "Summed handoff spans can overlap across producers; queue/body/return durations are wall time, not CPU usage or a guaranteed speedup.",
    "Last-five summaries follow ten initial requests; all 15 request records remain published."
  ],
